# GDPR Mobile Application Project

## 1) Identify the key personal data elements involved in the registration process for the mobile application. Based on the GDPR, explain why these data elements are considered personal data and require protection.

The key personal data elements collected as part of the registration process are **full name, date of birth, and email**. Based on GDPR, these elements collected as part of the registration process can identify an individual directly and hence can be considered personal data.

One more factor to consider here is whether the organisation is collecting data for EU citizens or not; this one factor can influence whether GDPR has to be considered or not. If EU citizens are considered for the data collection, then no matter where the data processor or related data controller is situated, both and multiple bodies, if involved, are subject to GDPR.

Finally, if data is collected for EU citizens and the data is digital, then GDPR needs to be complied with.

