## 2) Assess the legal basis for processing personal data in this mobile application project. Determine the most appropriate legal basis for collecting and processing users' personal data and provide a justification for your choice.

The legal basis for processing personal data in this case is specifically **legitimate interests**. The business wants to promote socialization among its employees; the reason for that is not stated explicitly in the case study but can be to create healthier work environments and promote more innovation or collaboration across employees at various levels within their respective domains.

However, it would be better if employees are given a clear-cut privacy policy update regarding why, how, and by what means the personal data of employees would be used and, finally, providing a proper **consent option** — not pre-checked checkboxes, nor compulsion, but a proper opportunity to opt out of data collection for the stated purpose would be helpful.

