## 5) Evaluate the risk of the project and provide an explanation as to why you chose that risk level. (Low/Medium/High/Very High)

I would say the risk level of the project is **Medium-High**, as the data elements that are being collected by the organisation are direct identifiers for individuals.

If these data elements are leaked or obtained by unethical means, then, in that case, the individuals can incur significant problems. Also, the data that is being collected is for the entire organisation, and hence the number of individuals is most probably greater, thus boosting the impact area of a privacy disaster.

The possibility of significant financial penalties is another factor that increases the risk of the project. Under the GDPR, certain infringements can result in administrative fines of up to **€20 million or 4% of the company's total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher**. Therefore, failure to implement appropriate GDPR compliance measures, whether intentionally or due to serious negligence, can expose the company to substantial financial and regulatory consequences.
